# Patent Claim Draft

**Claim 1**

A method for simultaneously transmitting analog and digital data across a galvanically isolated power transfer link, the method comprising:

receiving, at a transmitting side of the isolated power transfer link, an analog input signal representative of a sensed physical parameter;

converting the analog input signal into a variable-frequency pulse train using a voltage-to-frequency converter, wherein a pulse repetition rate of the pulse train is proportional to an instantaneous amplitude of the analog input signal;

receiving, at the transmitting side, a digital input data stream comprising a plurality of digital data bits;

encoding the digital input data stream by modulating a count of pulses within the pulse train over a plurality of defined counting intervals, such that a number of pulses occurring within each counting interval encodes at least one bit of the digital input data stream, while a total pulse count over a reference time period remains representative of the analog input signal;

combining the pulse train, having both the amplitude-proportional pulse frequency and the interval-based pulse-count encoding, into a composite pulse signal;

modulating a power carrier signal, generated for transferring electrical power across a galvanically isolated barrier, with the composite pulse signal to produce a combined power-and-data signal;

transmitting the combined power-and-data signal across the galvanically isolated barrier via a transformer, wherein the galvanically isolated barrier provides electrical isolation between the transmitting side and a receiving side while permitting inductive coupling of the combined power-and-data signal;

receiving, at the receiving side, the combined power-and-data signal;

extracting electrical power from the combined power-and-data signal to supply a load on the receiving side;

recovering the composite pulse signal from the combined power-and-data signal;

determining a pulse count occurring within each of the plurality of defined counting intervals from the recovered composite pulse signal to decode the digital data bits therefrom; and

determining an average pulse frequency of the recovered composite pulse signal over the reference time period to reconstruct the analog input signal;

whereby the analog input signal and the digital input data stream are simultaneously transmitted across the galvanically isolated power transfer link using event-count encoding of a single composite pulse signal superimposed on a transferred power carrier.

---

**Claim 2** (dependent, exemplary)

The method of claim 1, wherein encoding the digital input data stream comprises selectively adding or omitting at least one pulse within each of the defined counting intervals relative to a nominal pulse count corresponding to the analog input signal, such that the added or omitted pulse represents a binary digital data bit without altering the average pulse frequency over the reference time period by more than a predetermined tolerance.

**Claim 3** (dependent, exemplary)

The method of claim 1, wherein the galvanically isolated barrier comprises a single isolation transformer configured to transfer both the electrical power and the combined power-and-data signal across the isolation boundary.

**Claim 4** (dependent, exemplary)

The method of claim 1, further comprising synchronizing the plurality of defined counting intervals between the transmitting side and the receiving side using a periodic timing reference embedded within the composite pulse signal.
